Installation Instructions
=========================
Tarball
-------
The Linux tarball is a binary release. You can move this directory to any
suitable location such as `/opt/omeka-desktop-upload`, and start the
`omeka-desktop-upload` binary there.

In the following instructions, change `/opt/omeka-desktop-upload` to your
preferred location.

1. Move this directory to `/opt/omeka-desktop-upload`.
2. Add `/opt/omeka-desktop-upload` to your `PATH` environment variable.
3. Copy the icons:

   cp -r /opt/omeka-desktop-upload/resources/icons ~/.local/share/

4. Register the project file type (`.odu`):

   cp -r /opt/omeka-desktop-upload/resources/mime ~/.local/share/

5. Copy the `.desktop` and `.metainfo.xml` files:

   cp /opt/omeka-desktop-upload/org.omeka.DesktopUpload.desktop ~/.local/share/applications/
   cp /opt/omeka-desktop-upload/org.omeka.DesktopUpload.metainfo.xml ~/.local/share/metainfo/

6. And update the MIME and desktop databases:

   update-mime-database ~/.local/share/mime
   update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications/


Updating
========
When updating to a newer version,
replace the entire installation directory with the new one.


Dark Theme
==========
When using the dark theme you may want to use your GTK theme's dark variant.
After changing the theme, you will have to restart the application for the
window frame to update accordingly; if the menu or title bar don't use your
GTK theme's dark variant, try starting it with
`env GTK_THEME=Adwaita:dark omeka-desktop-upload` or your preferred theme.


Custom Themes
=============
You can adjust the user interface by placing files called `style-light.css`
and `style-dark.css` into your user-data folder (or just `style.css` for
adjusting all themes).


Sandbox
=======
The application requires your kernel to be configured with the options
`CONFIG_USER_NS` and `sysctl kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone=1`.

As a fallback, you can `sudo chown root chrome-sandbox` and
`chmod 4755 chrome-sandbox` to use the SETUID sandbox instead,
or start the application with the `--no-sandbox` flag.


Wayland
=======
By default, the application will use the X11 or XWayland windows.
For native Wayland use the following command line switches:

    omeka-desktop-upload --ozone-platform-hint=auto --enable-features=WaylandWindowDecorations

You can add those switches to your `.desktop` launcher as well.


System Libraries
================
The tarball includes the Electron platform and pre-compiled modules in
`resources/app.asar.unpacked/lib/node` and in
`resources/app.asar.unpacked/lib/vendor`.
The bundled image libraries are a prebuilt libvips; HEIC/HEIF images are not
supported.
